{"qid":"Q800","names":["Republic of Costa Rica"],"title":"Republic of Costa Rica","endonym":{"native":"República de Costa Rica","lang":"es"},"capsule":"The Republic of Costa Rica declared independence from Spain on 15 September 1821 as part of the Central American independence movement and briefly joined the First Mexican Empire before becoming part of the Federal Republic of Central America; it emerged as a fully sovereign republic in 1848. Coffee cultivation, introduced in the 1820s, transformed the economy and funded the construction of the Teatro Nacional (inaugurated 1897), while the 1889 presidential election—often cited as Central America's first genuinely free election—entrenched democratic norms. The country abolished its military by constitutional provision in 1948 following a brief civil war under José Figueres Ferrer, channeling defense expenditures into education and public health, and has sustained stable democratic governance since.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern Costa Rica's boundaries are well established by international treaties (particularly the 1858 Cañas-Jerez Treaty with Nicaragua and subsequent arbitrations); the 1840 start date in the atlas reflects the consolidation of sovereignty after federation dissolution.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Costa Rica","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costa_Rica"},{"label":"Britannica: Costa Rica","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Costa-Rica"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Costa Rica","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Costa_Rica"},{"label":"Wikipedia: José Figueres Ferrer","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jos%C3%A9_Figueres_Ferrer"}],"britannica":"place/Costa-Rica","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Costa Rica","rulers":[{"qid":"Q888888","name":"Braulio Carrillo Colina","start":1838,"end":1842,"image":"Braulio Carrillo.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Braulio%20Carrillo.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Lex.mercurio","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q886923","name":"Rafael Ángel Calderón Guardia","start":1840,"end":1844,"image":"Calderón Guardia 1940 cropped.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Calder%C3%B3n%20Guardia%201940%20cropped.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Harris-Ewing","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q880804","name":"José Rafael Gallegos","start":1845,"end":1846,"image":"José Rafael Gallegos Alvarado.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jos%C3%A9%20Rafael%20Gallegos%20Alvarado.JPG?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Aquiles Bigot","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"José Rafael Gallegos Alvarado","nativeLang":"es"},{"qid":"Q880785","name":"Juan Rafael Mora Porras","start":1849,"end":1859,"image":"Juan Rafael Mora Porras.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Juan%20Rafael%20Mora%20Porras.JPG?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Aquiles Bigot","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q2126914","name":"Rafael Barroeta Baca","start":1873,"end":1874,"image":null},{"qid":"Q762267","name":"Próspero Fernández Oreamuno","start":1882,"end":1885,"image":"Próspero Fernández Oreamuno.JPG","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pr%C3%B3spero%20Fern%C3%A1ndez%20Oreamuno.JPG?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Enrique Etheridge","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q767551","name":"Saturnino Lizano Gutiérrez","start":1882,"end":1882,"image":"Saturni